 <selectionEntry id="c614d693-ec9a-5ab0-9bf9-5ac013b7e17b" name="Fleet Construction Rules" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
 <profiles>
 </profiles>
 <rules><rule id="41a60845-8e47-5377-b608-08ada1bb7715" name="Fleet Construction" hidden="false"><description>Capital Ship allowance is generated by Line Ships: for every 4 individual Line Ships in the fleet you may include 1 Capital Ship. 0–3 Line Ships permit no Capital Ship; 4–7 permit 1; 8–11 permit 2; 12–15 permit 3, and so on — maximum Capital Ships = Line Ships ÷ 4, rounded down. Individual vessels count, not roster entries: a squadron of four Destroyers is four Line Ships. Line Ships are the Destroyer, Frigate, Light Cruiser, Assault Barge and Cruiser. Capital Ships are the Grand Cruiser, Battle Barge, Battleship, Emperor Battleship, Gloriana and Abyss, and the Phalanx above them. No single ship may exceed 50% of the fleet's points, upgrades included. Destroyers and Frigates have the Squadron keyword: each is taken singly, and up to 3 may be grouped into one squadron. Minimum game size: Gloriana 2,000; Abyss and Phalanx 3,000.</description></rule><rule id="36aa7c2c-db83-5fb5-9297-2181361db6d1" name="Ship Construction" hidden="false"><description>Ships are bought as a bare chassis and armed hardpoint by hardpoint. Every weapon and Defence Battery on a mount is paid for separately; Hangar Bay slots are built-in hull capacity and cost 0 pts. Each mount group shows its capacity — Defence Mounts 0/8, for instance — and you choose how many of that mount to fill. A hull filled with its standard armament costs exactly its rulebook price. There is no separate upgrade-spend ceiling: mount count and facing are the limits.</description></rule></rules><categoryLinks>
 <categoryLink id="149faf78-2ab8-5296-808a-2c09d662a11c" name="Rules" hidden="false" targetId="52616092-abd8-519e-a6fb-94b622114fa5" primary="true" /></categoryLinks>
 </selectionEntry>
 <selectionEntry id="2472afba-57fa-51b2-854a-3ea01d076f54" name="Fleet Orders" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade"><constraints><constraint type="max" value="1.0" field="selections" scope="force" shared="false" id="2cc9e478-bdcd-5e0f-98e1-b52002240ecd" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" /></constraints><rules><rule id="c5f7a745-80c5-53a0-832e-b0123b8cfe60" name="Fleet Orders" hidden="false"><description>Only the Flagship issues orders, within 24″ Command range measured from the Flagship as it stands, itself included. No order needs a test. Three types — Command, Movement, Shooting — each issued up to the number set by the commander's rank per round: Captain 1, Named Character 2, Primarch 3. No ship takes two orders of the same type in a round, ranks never combine, and nothing adds to the allowance. Unspent orders do not carry over. Command: Damage Control, Focus Fire, Brace for Impact. Movement: All Ahead Full, Burn Retros, Evade. Shooting: Reload Ordnance, Return Fire, Overwatch.</description></rule><rule id="cb09b292-78c0-5491-adee-99d5795d335c" name="Reactions" hidden="false"><description>Brace for Impact, Return Fire and Overwatch are Fleet Orders with a trigger, issued the moment a friendly ship is attacked or targeted, whether or not that ship has already acted. They count against the round's allowance however many ships are under fire — an order spent defending is one you no longer have for your own turn.</description></rule><rule id="c52e151f-9a27-5909-bd12-a38c98ea5cb1" name="Evade" hidden="false"><description>A Movement order, declared when the ship is shot at or rammed and before any dice are rolled. Roll a D6: on a 5+ the whole attack misses, or the ram fails and the rammer is moved 1″ past its intended victim. Modifiers: +1 Destroyer or Frigate · −1 held station · −1 Crippled, Adrift or Engines Crippled · −1 mounting no standard Macrobatteries. Never worse than −2. Once per battle round; wrecks and Speed 0 installations never Evade.</description></rule><rule id="b02aea4d-38ac-56a7-bb47-af78c006120c" name="Orders Need No Test" hidden="false"><description>No Fleet Order needs a test — the word is given and obeyed. There is no Morale, no Leadership and no test of a crew's nerve anywhere in the game; a damaged ship is measured by the Crippled and Depleted penalties alone. Command ranks instead carry their own abilities: Ship's Master, Practised Command, and the Primarch's own.</description></rule></rules><categoryLinks><categoryLink id="01f346cd-8fdd-5028-9a22-d59ed78db183" name="Rules" hidden="false" targetId="52616092-abd8-519e-a6fb-94b622114fa5" primary="true" /></categoryLinks></selectionEntry><selectionEntry id="60ad4905-a45a-55bc-9e12-461c456c1739" name="Phalanx" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="unit">
 <constraints>
